# debug client relationship notes

Starting these notes with the file header in `src/naf-dialog-adapter.js`. Dependencies for media transport, signaling, and an event emitter all appear here; from the name, it's easy to mistake `debug` for a standalone debugging entry point, but at this layer it's renamed after being imported.

```js
import * as mediasoupClient from "mediasoup-client";
import protooClient from "protoo-client";
import { debug as newDebug } from "debug";
import EventEmitter from "eventemitter3";
```

When reading this file, `newDebug` is a local name that needs to be kept distinct from the package name. `mediasoupClient`, `protooClient`, and `EventEmitter` appear in the same module header, which at least indicates that the adapter needs to interact with all these external objects. Not diagramming import order as call order yet; on the next pass, first check whether `newDebug` has any actual usage sites, then check the adjacent code to verify where the communication objects are wired in.

